> Converted from personal notes. Amounts are for one serving. Directions are editorial, not verified source instructions.

== Ingredients ==

Gather the following ingredients: @chicken breast{3/10%lb}, @dry quinoa{1/5%cup}, @large sweet potato{1/5} (cubed), @bell peppers{2/5} (sliced), @broccoli florets{2/5%cup}, @shelled edamame{1/5%cup}, @olive oil{2/5%tbsp}, @green onions{2/5} (sliced), @gluten-free tamari{3/5%tbsp}, @rice vinegar{2/5%tbsp}, @sesame oil{1/5%tbsp}, @honey{1/5%tbsp}, @grated ginger{1/5%tbsp}, @garlic cloves{2/5} (minced), @lime juice{1/5%tbsp}, @water{1/5%tbsp}.

== Preparation ==

Cook quinoa according to its package. Roast the sweet potato, peppers and broccoli with olive oil; cook chicken fully and slice. Whisk tamari, vinegar, sesame oil, honey, ginger, garlic, lime and water into a dressing. Assemble with edamame and green onion.
